<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 175 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 175 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 175 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    500 MLN    500 MLN    450 MLN    450 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    =	    270 MLN    445 MLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  T-BILLS	=	    =	    230 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    =	     40 MLN*   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE     =		=	  175 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
